PHP on Windows
==============
PHP has no official winget package with a predictable install path, so
windows_php.go handles it manually instead of going through the
generic InstallCommand flow:

  1. Downloads the official PHP zip for a pinned version/VC/arch combo
     from downloads.php.net (tries the current-releases path, then the
     archives path as a fallback).
  2. Extracts it to C:\tools\php, guarding against zip-slip path
     traversal on every entry.
  3. Appends the install dir to the user's PATH via setx (best
     effort if that fails, it prints the path so the user can add it
     manually).

installer.Install() checks for selectedOS == Windows && item.ID ==
"php" before the generic path and routes to InstallPHPWindows()
instead.

If you ever bump the pinned version, update the three constants at the
top of the file:

  phpVersion    = "8.4.22"
  phpVCVersion  = "vs17"
  phpArch       = "x64"
